WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.680
Captain! We should be in this fight.

2
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.690
You know that isn't an option.

3
00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:20.150
Even if we join them. none of our
weapons would deal any damage.

4
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.280
We don't have a choice in the matter.

5
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:26.120
It's in the hands of the hunters.

6
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.710
Stand your ground and fight!

7
00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:46.520
If they get past us.
the frontline's history!

8
00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.440
No! This is hopeless!

9
00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:08.000
Might've stood a chance if we
were higher ranked. but we're not!

10
00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.620
Damn it. I'm... fading fast!

11
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.100
Healing magic?

12
00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:29.100
Whoa. That worked instantly!

13
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:32.390
Hey. look out!

14
00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.220
Duck. Now!

15
00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:37.230
Go. Yoonho!

16
00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:38.510
Right!

17
00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:51.570
Yes. They're here.

18
00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.660
Leave it to the S-Rank
hunters to clean house!

19
00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:56.170
I think Byung-gu's
a little too eager.

20
00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.620
I'm sorry. but the sooner I act.
the more people I heal.

21
00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.540
Besides. I only rushed in the way I did
'cause you two were close behind.

22
00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.100
Hm.

23
00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:06.480
Huh?

24
00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:14.470
It's big. but I don't think
we've made it to the boss yet.

25
00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:17.770
Probably just the lead
pest of this infestation.

26
00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.940
Byung-gu. look after the wounded.

27
00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:22.390
Don't have to tell me twice.
I'm on it.

28
00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.190
Are you ready for this. Eunseok?

29
00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.740
You know it!

30
00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.980
-You're a tank. Damn.
-And?

31
00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.190
-Hm.
-Hm?

32
00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:03.770
This wasn't the leader after all.

33
00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.450
Lucky us.

34
00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.830
Seems they made it.

35
00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:21.710
No doubt in the nick of time.

36
00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:28.050
Well. well. Suppose we
should get started. too.

37
00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:30.260
Guild Master! On your order!

38
00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.720
Right.

39
00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:47.570
All units. attack!

40
00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:55.990
More than a decade ago. a
series of pathways appeared

41
00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:58.450
connecting our world
to another dimension.

42
00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:01.120
And ushering in untold horrors.

43
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:06.460
For the other side of these "gates" teamed
with bizarre creatures called "magic beasts."

44
00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:09.670
Though these monsters proved
immune to conventional weaponry.

45
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:12.920
some humans awakened abilities
to combat the threat.

46
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.630
They are known as hunters.

47
00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:18.060
And the magic coursing through
them determines their rank.

48
00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:25.220
There's S. A. B. C. D.
leaving E as the lowest level.

49
00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:31.520
The catch is: no amount of training
will improve their power once it awakens.

50
00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:35.210
A hunter's strength and rank
are set from day one.

51
00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.470
Best of luck to you and
your crew on today's raid.

52
00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:01.940
Thank you.

53
00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.150
Hey! What's up. Mr. Kim?

54
00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:06.650
Long time no see.

55
00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:09.900
Now there's a face
I wasn't expecting.

56
00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:13.290
Thought you said you'd had your
fill of hunting. Beom-shik.

57
00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.950
That was before baby
number two was on the way.

58
00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:20.410
A successful raid will definitely score
you a pretty nice mint for your new kiddo.

59
00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:22.570
Yeah. I'm pretty nervous.

60
00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:25.330
It's been a while.
So. you know. I'm super rusty.

61
00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:27.170
I was always weak to begin with.

62
00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:29.960
Huh? Is that a Jinwoo Sung I see?

63
00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:31.880
Yo. what's going on?

64
00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:34.130
Came out despite the cold. huh?

65
00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:35.720
Yeah.

66
00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:38.050
Nice to be working
with you guys again.

67
00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:39.680
Hey. kid. have you eaten yet?

68
00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.180
Can't fight magic beasts
running on fumes.

69
00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:45.560
Right. I did eat before
I got here. thanks.

70
00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.560
Why is everybody flagging him down?

71
00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.850
Is that kid like a
big deal or something?

72
00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:52.400
He's the exact opposite.

73
00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:54.860
Jinwoo joined up
not long after you quit.

74
00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:58.990
well. I call him the weakest
hunter of all mankind.

75
00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.490
Wait. really? That's a thing?

76
00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:05.790
It was once he got hospitalized
after a trip through an E-Rank gate.

77
00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:08.120
If that isn't weak.
then I don't know what is.

78
00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:11.000
It's hard to picture
of someone being that bad.

79
00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:15.090
But he is. So just him being here
means it's gonna be a real easy raid.

80
00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:16.630
Aha. Gotcha.

81
00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:20.610
We should probably drop it.
I'd hate for him to overhear us.

82
00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:24.220
Too late. Heard every word.

83
00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.810
Well. they didn't say anything
that isn't true. so I can't argue.

84
00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:30.440
Jinwoo! You got hurt again!

85
00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:32.480
Yeah. but I'll live.

86
00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.770
It's good to see you. Joohee.

87
00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:37.820
How about you skip the small talk
and explain what happened to you?

88
00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:39.150
Oh. I...

89
00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:41.990
You know. the same thing
that usually happens.

90
00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.580
You seriously need to be
more careful.

91
00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.750
I heard you even had a hospital stay.

92
00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:50.710
Hey. silver lining. though. is
that I was the only one hurt.

93
00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:52.830
So what exactly went wrong?

94
00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.880
The rest of the team was a higher-rank.
and the dungeon was an E.

95
00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:58.010
so they didn't think
to bring a healer.

96
00:06:58.090 --> 00:06:59.510
They didn't bring a healer?

97
00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:01.510
Of all the thoughtless.
self-centered things to do!

98
00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:04.930
Not like I'm mad. It isn't
their fault I'm so weak.

99
00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.850
I'm used to being treated
that way by hunters.

100
00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:10.400
-Figured you knew that.
-Hm.

101
00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:14.860
It looks like they're ready
to head inside. Come on.

102
00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:18.440
The name's Chiyul Song. and
unless any of you have objections.

103
00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:21.190
I volunteer to be the
leader of our dungeon raid.

104
00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:23.490
Speak now or hold your peace.

105
00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:25.040
Nope. I'm all for it.

106
00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.910
Chiyul is the most skilled
out of everybody here.

107
00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:30.080
One less worry if he's in charge.

108
00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:32.540
Working with you. sir.
is an absolute privilege.

109
00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.120
Thanks.

110
00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.050
Now. with that settled...

111
00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:37.470
Shall we?

112
00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:44.220
Hey. kid.

113
00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:48.060
Hang behind the rest of the
pack and don't get yourself hurt.

114
00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:49.970
Good idea. I'll try.

115
00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:52.440
Focus on succeeding. not trying.

116
00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:58.280
This knife has barely
any magic power in it.

117
00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:01.610
but it was the only weapon
I could afford.

118
00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:03.740
Hey. it's better than nothing.

119
00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:09.750
All right. let's see this
through to the end.

120
00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:20.680
Ah. welcome back. Chairman Go.

121
00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:24.130
How was your meeting
with the administration?

122
00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:26.760
We covered the usual talking points.

123
00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:29.180
Dungeon breaks
are a constant problem.

124
00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:33.190
but they still want the resources
we collect from every open gate.

125
00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:37.770
Their demands are logical.
Anyone with sense would agree.

126
00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.690
Hunting's now one of the most
lucrative careers on earth

127
00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:43.820
thanks to the treasures
found in those monster dens.

128
00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:51.620
Who would have guessed the
trophies inside magic beasts.

129
00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:54.910
these essence stones.
would be so valuable?

130
00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:02.750
I actually got one.

131
00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:04.340
I can hardly believe it.

132
00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:05.900
Jinwoo!

133
00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:23.030
-You have to fight him off!
-Stay back. Joohee!

134
00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:29.990
I gotta go back and help
with the main assault.

135
00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:31.870
Look after him and
patch him up if you can.

136
00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:33.410
Right. I will.

137
00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.580
You're going to be okay.

138
00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.260
I'll make you good as new.

139
00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:59.150
We hunters gather essence
stones from high ranked beasts

140
00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:01.600
and use them to create
weapons and armor.

141
00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:05.540
That allow us to take down even
more creatures in a vicious cycle.

142
00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:08.450
One would think we'd
just harvest mana crystals

143
00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:10.610
since they perform
the same function.

144
00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:13.240
Yet they're less potent
and make for weaker gear.

145
00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:16.420
But the government's interested
in a much different use?

146
00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:19.090
As a new power source. Yes.

147
00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:24.750
They're safer than nuclear. More
efficient than water. wind or geothermal.

148
00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:28.160
And don't pollute the
atmosphere like fossil fuels.

149
00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:31.510
Quite simply. the ideal clean energy.

150
00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:36.390
As we speak. scientists are working to get
those magic minerals to produce electricity.

151
00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:39.440
A rare fuel source only
hunters are able to collect.

152
00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:44.110
Making the burden that all hunters
bear heavier than it already was.

153
00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:53.370
We did it!

154
00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:57.670
I gotta hand it to you. Mr. Song.
you know how to call 'em!

155
00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:01.160
Now be honest. you aren't
just staying on as a hunter

156
00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:03.500
because you're too
stubborn to quit. right?

157
00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:07.970
It's only a matter of when. not if.
something much worse happens.

158
00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:11.220
I thought your stomach was all that
needed healing. but you're hurt everywhere!

159
00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:12.260
Sorry.

160
00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:14.970
I'm not asking for an
apology here. okay?

161
00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:16.730
I'm worried about you.

162
00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:25.060
Everyone. good?
All loot collected?

163
00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:27.570
If it can fetch a price.
safe to say we got it.

164
00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:30.440
Mana crystals are scarce
here as essence stones.

165
00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:33.240
This dungeon was one dry cash cow.

166
00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:36.540
I guess it's over.

167
00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:40.950
And all I have to show for it is
a single E-Rank essence stone.

168
00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:44.330
What a crap reward
for risking my life.

169
00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:47.460
Hey!

170
00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.840
Come take a look at this. guys!

171
00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.260
-A cave?
-Or tunnel maybe?

172
00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:54.760
Either way. it seems to go pretty far.

173
00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:58.520
This has to be a double dungeon.
Never seen one in person. though.

174
00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:01.520
I was wondering why there weren't
any signs of this place shutting down

175
00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:02.890
after we beat that mutt.

176
00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:05.650
I have to admit. that thought
crossed my mind. too.

177
00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:06.820
Then there's more.

178
00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:10.650
Maybe. this cash cow might
not be as dry as we assumed.

179
00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:12.650
Listen up. ladies and gents.

180
00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:16.740
Standard procedures is to report cases
like this to the Hunters Association.

181
00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:18.700
And wait for their approval.

182
00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:20.580
Now. hang on a second here.

183
00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:24.450
That'd give other hunters a chance
to beat the boss and loot the goods.

184
00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:28.250
There isn't any part of a D-Rank dungeon
that would be out of our group's league.

185
00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:29.630
He's got another kid on the way.

186
00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:32.590
He was banking on a
decent haul from this raid.

187
00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:35.470
It'd be okay to bend
the rules a tiny bit. right?

188
00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:36.810
Just a smidge?

189
00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:38.430
I understand how you feel.

190
00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:41.220
But going any farther
would endanger our lives.

191
00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:43.100
So I say we put it to a vote.

192
00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:45.060
-I'm not feeling it.
-Well. I am.

193
00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:47.440
-I vote no.
-Same here.

194
00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:48.770
It's worth checking out.

195
00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:50.270
-I agree.
-Me too.

196
00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:51.940
I-I beg to differ.

197
00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:54.320
-Come on. let's go.
-We'll be fine.

198
00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:57.300
I'm sorry. everyone.
I really don't want to.

199
00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:01.160
All right. That's six in favor
of going and six opposed.

200
00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:03.910
Which would make Jinwoo here
the deciding vote.

201
00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:06.010
What. i-it's up to me?

202
00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:11.470
Even if the danger isn't above a
D-Rank. I'm in trouble no matter what.

203
00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:15.000
Still with Dad missing.

204
00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:17.800
I'm the only one
who can provide for my family.

205
00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:19.680
Mom's treatments aren't free.

206
00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:22.180
And then there's
my sister's college tuition.

207
00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:26.520
I don't want money. I need it.

208
00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:28.040
I vote yes.

209
00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:38.370
Raise your right hand. place it on
a black crystal and just try to relax.

210
00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:46.710
We're ready for whoever's next.

211
00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:53.580
We would love a C-Rank hunter
such as yourself to join our guild.

212
00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:56.250
Just look at that bottom section
and you'll find our labor conditions

213
00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:57.950
listed in extensive detail.

214
00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:05.440
As of right now. a B-Rank hunter and
two C-Ranks agreed to sign with our guild.

215
00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:07.450
So it's going rather well. I'd say.

216
00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:10.150
I think you'll be
pleased. Guild Master.

217
00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:11.980
I already am.

218
00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:14.520
If anybody seems like an asset.
make them an offer

219
00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:16.990
regardless of their age or gender.

220
00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:19.570
I doubt they'll compare to
someone like Hae-in Cha.

221
00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:21.670
but the world is full of surprises.

222
00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:25.750
Purse thieves! Stop them!

223
00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.830
Outta the damn way!

224
00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:29.170
Holy!

225
00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:31.570
Huh?!

226
00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:34.050
Move. lady! D'you wanna die?

227
00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:58.370
-Gosh. that was incredible.
-Here.

228
00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:00.910
Thank you.
Thank you so much.

229
00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:05.370
The S-Rank hunter?

230
00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:08.960
I'd like to leave.

231
00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:16.590
Look at her go!

232
00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:18.890
That's an S-Rank hunter for you.

233
00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:23.880
How long's it been
since we started this trek?

234
00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:25.680
About 40 minutes.

235
00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:30.770
Gates close an hour after the boss is
defeated. so we'll have 20 minutes to spare.

236
00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:32.890
Joohee. I'm really sorry.

237
00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:34.430
What'd you do now?

238
00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:36.320
I voted yes to come down here.

239
00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:38.740
Even though you hoped
that we'd call it quits.

240
00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:42.190
I'm the last thing you should
be worried about. so stop it.

241
00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:44.940
I'll stop if you're sure you're okay.

242
00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:46.700
You've got to be kidding me.

243
00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:50.120
I'm obviously not okay.
Get a sudden case of amnesia?

244
00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:52.370
Or has it not occurred to you
that goblin could've struck

245
00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:54.370
a little higher and ended your life?

246
00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:58.210
Healing up that wound along with
your arms and legs wasn't easy. Jinwoo!

247
00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.920
I swear you hit your head.

248
00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.460
That's the only explanation for
how much of an idiot you're being!

249
00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:05.050
I'm sorry.

250
00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:06.310
I can't deny.

251
00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:10.470
Joohee's B-Rank healing spells have
come in clutch on more than one occasion.

252
00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:12.680
Do you really grasp the issue here?

253
00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.230
Yeah.

254
00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:18.110
Well. in that case. you could
always show your thanks

255
00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:20.070
by taking me out to eat somewhere.

256
00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:24.400
Why the shock? Is the thought of
treating me to a meal so upsetting to you?

257
00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:26.790
No. no. no. no. no.
That's not it at all.

258
00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:29.080
Finally! We found the lair!

259
00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:34.450
Rare to see an actual door
on one of these.

260
00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:36.300
It's kind of unnerving.

261
00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:37.750
Mm-hm.

262
00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:40.920
Didn't walk that marathon
to turn back empty-handed.

263
00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.420
No. sure as heck didn't.

264
00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:47.160
The team moves forward
together. All 13 of us.

265
00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:48.890
Isn't that right?

266
00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.310
Yep. That's the deal.

267
00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:57.270
For those who don't know me.
I'm Gunhee Go.

268
00:16:57.350 --> 00:17:00.520
Greetings from the Hunter's
Association's current chair.

269
00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:04.270
Some of you newly awakened will
choose to become hunters. Some won't.

270
00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:07.250
But I ask that you consider
carefully before deciding.

271
00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:11.490
It's been ten years since the gates
appeared. yet they still remain a mystery

272
00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:12.830
for the most part.

273
00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:15.630
So to become a hunter
is to risk your life.

274
00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:18.790
Even those accustomed to raids
cannot let their guards down.

275
00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:21.380
Refrain from growing
arrogant or careless.

276
00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:24.590
My best advice to ensure
your survival would be:

277
00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:26.770
stay both humble and afraid.

278
00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:36.770
Heh. "Let there be light."

279
00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:38.360
And a dope atmosphere.

280
00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:40.690
This dungeon's unique all right.

281
00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:51.740
What's with the old statues?

282
00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:53.740
They each have something different.

283
00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:56.210
Yeah. a weapon or an instrument.

284
00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:57.800
Oh. whoa.

285
00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:04.210
He makes the others seem like toys.

286
00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:05.930
That's damn huge.

287
00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:08.800
-He a king?
-King of creepiness.

288
00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:11.470
So where are the mana crystals
and magic beasts?

289
00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:14.470
I'm saying I don't even see bugs.

290
00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:18.060
What's this for? Divination?

291
00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:20.820
Mister Song!
Something's written over here.

292
00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:24.900
In ancient script. of course.

293
00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:27.990
"The Cartenon Temple's
Commandments are as follows."

294
00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:30.950
"First. thou shalt worship God."

295
00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:33.620
-"Second. thou shalt praise God."
-J-Jinwoo!

296
00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:36.830
"Third. thou shalt prove thy faith."

297
00:18:36.910 --> 00:18:41.420
That huge stone statue.
I saw its eyes move.

298
00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:44.120
It's been watching us
this entire time.

299
00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:45.500
Uh...

300
00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:49.130
There's no way.
You're seeing things.

301
00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:51.390
"You will not leave alive?"

302
00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:58.190
The door! It just shut on its own!

303
00:18:58.270 --> 00:18:59.810
-But why?
-It's fine.

304
00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:02.190
I'm sure we can open it
back up again.

305
00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:04.190
Better hope so.

306
00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:07.150
See. this is what we get
for taking a stupid risk.

307
00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:10.580
I knew we shouldn't have
kept going. but I was outvoted.

308
00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:14.650
If there's treasure lying around.
you idiots are welcome to it.

309
00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:16.590
I'm leaving.

310
00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:19.130
Look out. it's a trap!

311
00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:39.640
-Didn't stand a chance.
-They'll get us. too!

312
00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:42.650
What now?
Do we fight those things?

313
00:19:43.850 --> 00:19:47.440
That guy who died.
he must've been D-Rank at least.

314
00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:51.070
Stronger than me. anyway.
I mean. who isn't?

315
00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:55.190
And he was gone. Just like that.

316
00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:58.120
What's going on?
This is a D-Rank dungeon.

317
00:19:58.200 --> 00:20:01.080
No. no. there aren't supposed
to be things like that down here.

318
00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:04.710
If these statues are moving.
then that means...

319
00:20:18.390 --> 00:20:22.850
I've stared death in the face plenty
of times since I became a hunter.

320
00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:27.360
In my first raid. I lost my
party and wound up stranded.

321
00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:30.730
E-Rank monsters have
hospitalized me for weeks.

322
00:20:30.810 --> 00:20:33.980
There was a time I nearly
starved to death in a labyrinth.

323
00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.620
It could be the lowest
of low-ranked dungeons.

324
00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.750
but I'll still be
fighting for my life.

325
00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:44.330
Most hunters buy upgraded gear with the
cash they make from selling essence stones.

326
00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:48.010
They take down stronger
beasts. reap bigger rewards.

327
00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:51.710
But I break the bank just
splurging on cheap knives.

328
00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:53.550
and once they break. that's it.

329
00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:55.720
I'm back to fighting
with my bare hands.

330
00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:58.770
Even my shoes are shot.

331
00:20:59.430 --> 00:21:02.690
And so. day after excruciating day...

332
00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:07.770
...I endure the mockery
and perform this

333
00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:11.190
life-threatening job that
takes way more than it gives.

334
00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:14.070
'Cause I've learned that
I can survive most anything.

335
00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:16.990
if I keep my eyes
peeled for opportunities.

336
00:21:17.070 --> 00:21:19.460
Maybe that's why I was able to tell.

337
00:21:20.070 --> 00:21:21.500
Get down now!

338
00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:38.180
What the hell?

339
00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:40.180
-For real.
-How'd we trigger it?

340
00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:42.470
-You think I know?
-Are you all right. Beom-shik?

341
00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:44.600
Somehow. What about you?

342
00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:45.770
I'm fine.

343
00:21:45.850 --> 00:21:47.360
No more.

344
00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:48.740
Please. no more!

345
00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:51.690
What just happened?

346
00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:54.150
This can't be real.

347
00:21:55.020 --> 00:21:56.580
But it is. we're trapped.

348
00:21:57.320 --> 00:21:58.620
Done for.

349
00:21:59.650 --> 00:22:00.950
Dead.

350
00:22:02.950 --> 00:22:04.750
We're all gonna die!
